{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3cdd126c-42c1-40b8-aeed-c4ad050fe9c9","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A derivative measures a curve’s slope at one point. Start with the parabola and the point where x equals one.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Derivative = tangent slope"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,2.3],"y":[-1,5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"curve","y":"x^2","domain":[0,2.2],"label":"y = x²"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"on":"curve","x":1},"label":"P (1, 1)"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3cdd126c-42c1-40b8-aeed-c4ad050fe9c9","step":{"id":"s2","script":"A second point gives a secant line. Its slope is the change in height divided by the change in x.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"secant","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"q","at":{"on":"curve","x":2},"label":"Q (2, 4)"},{"kind":"segment","id":"pq","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":[2,1],"stroke":"dashed","label":"Δx = 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,1],"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed","label":"Δy = 3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"secantslope","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"m_{\\mathrm{sec}}=\\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}=2+h"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3cdd126c-42c1-40b8-aeed-c4ad050fe9c9","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Move the second point closer. As h approaches zero, the secant slopes approach two, giving the tangent’s slope.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"near","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"qnear","at":{"on":"curve","x":1.3}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"qnear"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"tangent","id":"tan","to":"curve","x":1,"length":0.85,"label":"tangent"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"limit","anchor":{"el":"secantslope","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"f'(1)=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2+h)=2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What does f′(1) = 2 tell you about the tangent at P?","expected_gist":"The tangent at (1,1) has slope 2: it rises 2 units for each unit to the right."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3cdd126c-42c1-40b8-aeed-c4ad050fe9c9","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The tangent passes through one, one with slope two. Its equation describes the straight line that matches the curve’s local direction.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"slopeguide","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":[1.5,1],"stroke":"dashed","label":"0.5"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1.5,1],"to":[1.5,2],"stroke":"dashed","label":"1"},{"kind":"point","at":[1.5,2]}]},{"op":"equation","id":"taneq","anchor":{"el":"limit","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"y-1=2(x-1)\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y=2x-1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
